/// What an edge reports after it verified (or refused) a distributed bundle.
/// 07 "Policy bundles": "The ACK ledger is the other half of distribution: the
/// edge reports which seq it verified and activated, and the canary query below
/// is the only input the rollout controller trusts, because 'we pushed it' is a
/// claim and 'the device ACKed it' is a record."
///
/// Field set is 05 §4.3's: "(channel, seq, bundle_hash, result:
/// applied|rejected|partial, sections_skipped\[\], reject_code)". The same section
/// then states what is NOT in the body — "the ledger row adds `device_id` (from
/// the token stamp), `edge_version`, and `acked_at`" — so those three are
/// server-derived from the authenticated request and are absent here by design;
/// a client-supplied device_id would be the trust-boundary mistake 07 §2's
/// advisory-field note exists to prevent.
///
